  "notes": "Cash basis. Governmental lines from Statement of Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balances (Total Governmental Funds, p5); business-type from the proprietary fund statement (p7). Governmental roll: 237,293 + 1,156,439 - 965,053 + 650,426 - 576,373 + 715,000 + 7,381 = 1,225,113. Business roll: 31,753 + 339,513 - 590,484 + 310,000 - 74,053 = 16,729. Bond proceeds treated as business debt_proceeds; capital contribution (85,604) kept as a nonoperating receipt as printed (budget schedule p8 counts it under Intergovernmental). Business-type receipts total is not printed, so summed (computed). The only detail schedule (p8, Budgetary Comparison Schedule) combines governmental and proprietary funds in one column; it is recorded in detail (fund 'All funds'), with the mixed lines (Intergovernmental, Local, Debt proceeds, Debt service, Transfers out) split by fund type using the p5/p7 statements (split_from); budget_final is left null on split parts because the budget is printed only for the combined line. Balance sheet is the government-wide total column; the total column of the statement of net position has no liabilities. Pages 2-3 are the government-wide statement of activities (not used for lines). Read pages 1-8 of 8. Detail (user 2026-10-27): per-fund lines from the fund statements' columns (p5, p7) replace the combined schedule."
